\pard\sb180\sa160\b\fs31 Transaction Analysis Flow: Kafka \u8594? Antifraud \u8594? Signature Service\b0\par
\pard\sa100\fs19 STORAGE source: SEQUENCE_EXAMPLES.docx, Example #3, titled Transaction Analysis Flow. The source includes a repeated PlantUML sequence with four participants: Integration Platform, Kafka, Antifraud and a named signing provider. The public edition retains the flow but replaces the named signing vendor with Signature Service.\b0\par
\pard\sb200\sa100\b\fs25 Main source flow\b0\par
\pard\sa100\fs19 1. Integration platform puts a transaction-analysis request on Kafka.\b0\par
\pard\sa100\fs19 2. Antifraud consumes the request.\b0\par
\pard\sa100\fs19 3. On a technical processing failure, the message is routed to a DLQ.\b0\par
\pard\sa100\fs19 4. On success, antifraud evaluates risk/rules and publishes a decision, score and triggered-rule details.\b0\par
\pard\sa100\fs19 5. The integration platform consumes the response.\b0\par
\pard\sa100\fs19 6. If the platform cannot process the response, it publishes a DLQ record.\b0\par
\pard\sa100\fs19 7. The platform prepares the downstream customer/partner result.\b0\par
\pard\sa100\fs19 8. It requests signing from an external signature service.\b0\par
\pard\sa100\fs19 9. The signature service returns a signed result or file reference.\b0\par
\pard\sa100\fs19 Source-quality clarification: The original step 1 says \u8220?creates a topic for transaction analysis\u8221?. This appears to describe publishing a message to a pre-existing Kafka topic, not provisioning a fresh topic for each payment. The public sequence uses the latter interpretation explicitly as a correction, not a claim about the historical source.\b0\par
\pard\sb200\sa100\b\fs25 Participants and message ownership\b0\par
\pard\li180\sa75\fs18 Component  |  Ownership\b0\par
\pard\li180\sa75\fs18 Integration Platform  |  Create correlated request, consume result, invoke signer\b0\par
\pard\li180\sa75\fs18 Kafka  |  Transport analysis request/response across consumer groups\b0\par
\pard\li180\sa75\fs18 Antifraud  |  Risk evaluation and decision result\b0\par
\pard\li180\sa75\fs18 Signature Service  |  Sign normalized response under a valid contract\b0\par
\pard\li180\sa75\fs18 Operations / DLQ  |  Control poison-message review and safe redrive\b0\par
\pard\sb200\sa100\b\fs25 Example event envelope (fictional)\b0\par
\pard\li240\sa75\fs19 \u8226? eventId: unique delivery identity\b0\par
\pard\li240\sa75\fs19 \u8226? transactionReference: opaque correlation to payment/analysis attempt\b0\par
\pard\li240\sa75\fs19 \u8226? analysisResult: APPROVE, REVIEW or REJECT\b0\par
\pard\li240\sa75\fs19 \u8226? riskScore: numeric outcome if allowed by contract\b0\par
\pard\li240\sa75\fs19 \u8226? rulesTriggered: non-sensitive rule references\b0\par
\pard\sa100\fs19 Do not expose confidential fraud rules, raw PAN, authentication material or user identifiers in public Kafka event samples.\b0\par
\pard\sb200\sa100\b\fs25 Failure and security review (new)\b0\par
\pard\li240\sa75\fs19 \u8226? Require durable consume-before-offset-commit behavior with consumer inbox dedupe.\b0\par
\pard\li240\sa75\fs19 \u8226? Distinguish transient technical errors from final business fraud decisions.\b0\par
\pard\li240\sa75\fs19 \u8226? Route DLQ only after durable quarantine handoff, with correlation and operations ownership.\b0\par
\pard\li240\sa75\fs19 \u8226? Do not silently generate a client success response if antifraud or signing status is unknown.\b0\par
\pard\li240\sa75\fs19 \u8226? Verify signing provider authorization, response format, nonrepudiation requirements and timeout handling.\b0\par
